spec = ofpbuf_put_zeros(ofpacts, sizeof *spec);
error = learn_parse_spec(orig, name, value, port_map, spec, ofpacts, &match);
```

The `spec` pointer becomes stale if `learn_parse_spec` calls `ofpbuf_put_zeros(ofpacts, ...)` internally (which it does for immediate values)! After reallocation, `spec` points to freed/old memory, and the learn spec data might be corrupted.

