uint8_t *src_imm = ofpbuf_put_zeros(ofpacts, OFPACT_ALIGN(imm_bytes));
memcpy(src_imm, &imm, imm_bytes);
```

The comment says "Push value last, as this may reallocate 'spec'!" - so they know about this issue. The spec fields are set before this reallocation, so it should be OK because the data is already written to the buffer before reallocation (the spec is at a fixed offset within the ofpbuf, so the data moves together with the buffer).

Wait - actually when `ofpbuf_put_zeros` extends the buffer, if reallocation happens, the old buffer content is copied to the new location. So the spec data (which was written to the old spec pointer) is preserved in the new location. The pointer `spec` itself becomes stale, but since we don't use it after the reallocation in `learn_parse_spec` (for the immediate case), it's fine.

